# Wendi's Level 2: Portal Lift
# Send the boulder through the portal, follow it down the slide, and leave it on
# the floor button. Its weight powers both the fan and the spike-sided platforms.
script portal_lift
bounds 0 0 1600 900
playerStart 72 780

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GUIDE-AUTHORED INDUSTRIAL TILE ART
# The far-background mask covers the entire visible chamber, including the
# open portal chute and lower fan course. Foreground architecture below traces
# only solid boundaries; physics remains defined by the unchanged records.
visualTileRect farBackground 0 0 0 0 50 27
# Keep the starting-room foundation interior black while continuing the open
# chamber mask through the portal chute and the lower-right traversal space.
visualTileRect farBackground 0 0 320 864 39 1

# Deliberate blue depth panels use the guide's 16px-offset background grid.
# Starting-room service recess.
visualTile background 0 0 80 80
visualTile background 1 0 112 80
visualTile background 2 0 144 80
visualTile background 0 1 80 112
visualTile background 1 1 112 112
visualTile background 2 1 144 112
visualTile background 0 3 80 144
visualTile background 1 3 112 144
visualTile background 2 3 144 144

# Broad machinery recess behind the portal arrival and ramp.
visualTile background 0 0 880 80
visualTileRect background 1 0 912 80 5 1
visualTile background 2 0 1072 80
visualTile background 0 1 880 112
visualTileRect background 1 1 912 112 5 1
visualTile background 2 1 1072 112
visualTile background 0 3 880 144
visualTileRect background 1 3 912 144 5 1
visualTile background 2 3 1072 144

# Vertical service panel behind the catch basin.
visualTile background 3 0 1456 208
visualTileRect background 3 1 1456 240 1 5
visualTile background 3 3 1456 400

# Lower-room structural recesses behind the airborne route.
visualTile background 0 0 944 688
visualTileRect background 1 0 976 688 4 1
visualTile background 2 0 1104 688
visualTile background 0 3 944 720
visualTileRect background 1 3 976 720 4 1
visualTile background 2 3 1104 720
visualTile background 0 0 1232 688
visualTileRect background 1 0 1264 688 5 1
visualTile background 2 0 1424 688
visualTile background 0 3 1232 720
visualTileRect background 1 3 1264 720 5 1
visualTile background 2 3 1424 720

# Exterior top edge is a ceiling because the playable room lies below it.
visualTile foreground 4 0 0 0
visualTileRect foreground 1 3 32 0 48 1
visualTile foreground 5 0 1568 0

# Exterior walls face inward toward the open room.
visualTileRect foreground 2 2 0 32 1 27
visualTileRect foreground 0 2 1568 32 1 27

# The divider separating the starting room uses the thin vertical strip.
visualTile foreground 3 0 430 28
visualTileRect foreground 3 1 430 60 1 25
visualTile foreground 3 3 430 860

# Starting-room foundation: one walkable top row with intentional mass below.
visualTile foreground 0 1 28 840
visualTileRect foreground 1 1 60 840 7 1
visualTile foreground 2 1 284 840

# Portal-chute wall uses vertical strip pieces rather than stacked floor tiles.
visualTile foreground 3 0 325 560
visualTileRect foreground 3 1 325 592 1 8
visualTile foreground 3 3 325 848

# The dark rail chamber is capped by a correctly oriented visible ceiling.
visualTile foreground 0 3 458 160
visualTileRect foreground 1 3 490 160 8 1
visualTile foreground 2 3 746 160

# Arrival basin: thin landing surface and inward-facing retaining wall.
visualTile foreground 0 0 995 420
visualTileRect foreground 1 0 1027 420 9 1
visualTile foreground 5 1 1315 420
visualTile foreground 0 2 1320 330
visualTile foreground 0 2 1320 362
visualTile foreground 0 2 1320 394

# The upper hazard shelf is a single platform row, not a filled foundation.
visualTile foreground 0 0 925 590
visualTileRect foreground 1 0 957 590 18 1
visualTile foreground 2 0 1533 590

# Enclosed starting room. The upper ledge is split around the ladder so the
# player can climb through it instead of colliding with its underside.
solid 0 0 1600 28
solid 0 28 28 872
solid 430 28 28 872
solid 28 840 297 60
platform 48 510 20 30
platform 118 510 232 30
ladder 68 510 48 330
boulder 292 472 27 3.2

# This wall blocks the ground-level shortcut to the orange entrance. The ball
# and player must cross the upper ledge and drop into the portal chute.
solid 325 560 20 340
portalPair 345 790 80 48 735 45 120 22

# The blue outlet drops both bodies onto the upper ramp. The boulder rolls into
# the expanded catch basin and remains on its persistent floor switch. The long
# landing leaves enough clear space after the slide for the player to pass.
ramp 890 257 335 30 30 3
solid 995 420 353 40
solid 1320 330 28 130
button 1240 404 80 16

# Button 0 illuminates the otherwise dark rail chamber. The floor fan rests on
# a dedicated maintenance plinth rather than floating above the lower room.
fan 850 835 0 -1 505 120 2500 0
platform 814 858 72 30

# Six spike-sided platforms always circulate around a fixed steel rail. They
# exist in the darkness even before the first button turns the chamber light on.
buttonPlatformLoop -1 630 585 55 270 72 30 24 6
darkness 458 188 302 712
# A masonry ceiling visually encloses the dark rail chamber. A powered hanging
# lamp is rendered above the rail when Button 0 illuminates the room. Both the
# ceiling and darkness meet the starting-room divider without leaving a gap.
solid 458 160 302 28

# Button 1 rides on the lower-left rail platform. Once stepped on, it
# latches the fan on and unlocks the exit door.
platformLoopButton 0 2 62 12
buttonFan 1 0 1
buttonExit 1

# The broad shelf extends over the exit so the player cannot bypass the course
# by dropping onto the door from above. It is safe on top but has
# downward-facing spikes below. A patrol robot guards the upper route.
solid 925 590 647 24
directionalSpikeHazard down 925 614 647 28
enemy 1120 550 34 40 990 1400 70

# Four narrow, staggered platforms carry the airborne player beneath the spike
# shelf and toward the final exit ledge.
platform 950 770 72 30
platform 1090 810 72 30
platform 1230 755 72 30
platform 1370 800 72 30
platform 1450 825 150 32
solid 1572 28 28 872
exit 1490 625 82 200
